You mean *API calls* to test if GitHub is working, right?

Fastest test from your phone/terminal:

*1. Check basic API access*
curl -i https://api.github.com/user

This should return `401 Unauthorized` - that’s normal. It means the API is up, you just didn’t send a token.

*2. Test with your account*
Generate a Personal Access Token first: GitHub menu → *Settings* → *Developer settings* → *Personal access tokens* → *Tokens (classic)* → Generate new token.

Then run:
curl -H "Authorization: token YOUR_TOKEN" https://api.github.com/user

If it returns your user info with `"login": "Lockincreate"`, auth + API calls are working.

*3. Test repo access*
curl -H "Authorization: token YOUR_TOKEN" https://api.github.com/repos/Lockincreate/REPO_NAME

Replace `REPO_NAME` with one of your repos. 200 OK = all good.

